   "title": "IDEA-151 · Calculate what an empty shelf costs you",
   "original_idea": "[IDEA-151] Calculate what an empty shelf costs you\nCarousel · P2 Pain & cost\n\nObjective:\nanswers Why · Light theme · when: Before White Friday or Ramadan\n\nHook (EN):\nWhat does an empty shelf cost you?\n\nHook (AR):\nقدّيش بيكلّفك الرفّ الفاضي؟\n\nScene plan:\nSupport line (EN):\nDo the maths with your own numbers.\n\nOn-image elements (HTML layer):\nCover OB-37; formula slides with blank boxes to fill.\n\nSlides (carousels):\n1. What does an empty shelf cost you?\n2. Sales lost per day × days out of stock.\n3. × your margin on that item.\n4. + the customers who buy elsewhere next time.\n5. = the real cost. Usually more than the stock itself.\n6. Comment COST and we'll send you the calculator.\n\nImages:\nOB-37 · BG-57\n\nConversion mechanic:\nComment \"COST\" → DM sheet\n\nKPI to watch:\nComments with keyword, DMs\n\nNotes:\nPrepare the calculator sheet before posting.\n\nCaption:\nNo industry averages. Your numbers, your answer.\nComment COST and we'll DM you a simple calculator sheet.",
