   "title": "IDEA-162 · Reorder point, explained",
   "original_idea": "[IDEA-162] Reorder point, explained\nCarousel · P3 How it works & know-how\n\nObjective:\nLight theme · when: Any time\n\nHook (EN):\nWhen should you reorder?\n\nHook (AR):\nإيمتى لازم تعيد الطلب؟\n\nScene plan:\nSupport line (EN):\nThe reorder point, explained with one import example.\n\nOn-image elements (HTML layer):\nFormula card: daily sales × lead time + safety stock.\n\nSlides (carousels):\n1. When should you reorder?\n2. Daily sales × lead time + safety stock.\n3. Example: 10 a day × 35 days by sea + 50 extra = 400.\n4. When you hit 400, the next order should already be leaving.\n5. Stacko's low-stock alerts tell you when you reach your minimum.\n\nImages:\nBG-57\n\nConversion mechanic:\nSaves\n\nKPI to watch:\nSaves\n\nNotes:\nDo not say Stacko calculates reorder points (roadmap).\n\nCaption:\nMost stockouts start months earlier, on the day nobody reordered. Save this one.",
